28
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:15,500
Let's explore why it is in the next part, sample analysis and improvements.

29
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:26,860
Firstly, the format of the essay is the first aspect that influences the task response band score.

30
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:36,160
An appropriate format at band 6.0 plus must ensure a complete essay with three parts,

31
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,780
introduction, body, and conclusion.

32
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:43,500
The essay should be at least 250 words long.

33
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:48,480
Considering these two aspects, the essay has quite

34
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:52,840
a good structure, but does not meet the requirement of the length.

35
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:57,680
With only 213 words, this essay is too short

36
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:03,040
leading to a lower task response score for under length.

37
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:08,320
Therefore, when improving this essay, you should consider these factors.

38
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,280
Now, let's go through each part of the essay.

39
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:13,600
Introduction.

40
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,160
For agree or disagree essays, to write an introduction 

41
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:22,900
at band 6.0 plus for task response, we need to do two things.

42
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:29,980
Write a general statement by paraphrasing the question to remind the reader about the topic of the essay.

43
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:35,580
Ensure that thesis statement states the writer's opinion on the given topic.

44
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:39,500
Now, let's read the introduction and see if

45
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:41,800
it has completed the two tasks or not.

46
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:07,630
It is argued that schools should teach students

47
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:10,790
to be good people apart from providing formal education.

48
00:04:11,370 --> 00:04:15,190
This is the general statement and it paraphrases the question.

49
00:04:16,050 --> 00:04:19,550
I completely agree with this statement because of the following reasons.

50
00:04:20,290 --> 00:04:24,650
This thesis statement states the writer's opinion on the given topic.

51
00:04:25,290 --> 00:04:30,050
The introduction of the sample is good enough to achieve band 6 for task response.

52
00:04:31,010 --> 00:04:37,970
However, as mentioned earlier, instead of choosing one side and focusing solely on it, 

53
00:04:37,970 --> 00:04:41,730
we should write about both sides and choose one side to support more.

54
00:04:42,450 --> 00:04:46,270
Therefore, we should rewrite the introduction as follows.

55
00:04:46,990 --> 00:04:49,290
It is argued that schools should teach students

56
00:04:49,290 --> 00:04:52,690
to be good people apart from providing formal education.

57
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:57,490
Although behavioral education is not entirely school's responsibility,

58
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:01,510
I still think that it is the responsibility of schools.

59
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:05,790
So, in this thesis statement, we only partly

60
00:05:05,790 --> 00:05:08,170
agree with the topic and we will develop

61
00:05:08,170 --> 00:05:11,030
two following ideas in the body paragraphs.

62
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:16,970
Teaching children good behaviors is not entirely the responsibility of schools.

63
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:22,050
Schools still have some responsibility to teach children good behaviors.

64
00:05:23,130 --> 00:05:25,450
We'll support the second idea more.

65
00:05:25,970 --> 00:05:29,750
The schools still have some responsibility to teach children good behaviors.

66
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:33,570
Today, we're only focusing on task response.

67
00:05:34,090 --> 00:05:36,850
In the lesson on lexical resource, we'll learn

68
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:41,370
about some effective structures to apply to introduction of this type.

69
00:05:42,850 --> 00:05:46,490
Now, let's analyze body paragraph 1 to see

70
00:05:46,490 --> 00:05:48,870
if it actually supports the main opinion.

71
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:52,470
The writer argues that schools are responsible for

72
00:05:52,470 --> 00:05:57,770
teaching manners because children spend a significant amount of time at school.

73
00:05:58,150 --> 00:06:01,330
They explain that students spend hours with teachers

74
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:05,930
and give an example of students spending seven hours on campus.

75
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:09,070
However, there is a logical gap here.

76
00:06:09,530 --> 00:06:15,250
The paragraph proves that children are at school for a long time but it fails to

77
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:19,910
explain why that time creates a responsibility to teach behavior.

78
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:24,530
It describes the situation but misses the link to the topic.

79
00:06:25,550 --> 00:06:31,030
This is a common mistake, describing facts without linking them to the argument.

80
00:06:31,670 --> 00:06:34,350
Now, let's look at body paragraph 2.

81
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:37,090
The main argument here is about money.

82
00:06:37,610 --> 00:06:40,310
Parents pay tuition fees so they expect a

83
00:06:40,310 --> 00:06:43,310
return on investment, which is that they want

84
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:46,530
their children to become good and successful individuals.

85
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:48,830
But look at this sentence.

86
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:52,270
Also, parents gave birth to their children.

87
00:06:52,710 --> 00:06:54,230
I have a question for you.

88
00:06:54,630 --> 00:06:55,910
Is this relevant?

89
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:59,970
Does the biological fact of giving birth relate

90
00:06:59,970 --> 00:07:02,430
to tuition fees or school responsibility?

91
00:07:02,950 --> 00:07:04,830
The answer is no.

92
00:07:05,310 --> 00:07:08,030
This sentence is completely off-topic.

93
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:10,530
It breaks the flow of the argument.

94
00:07:11,810 --> 00:07:15,310
Therefore, we have two common mistakes that will

95
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:20,410
keep your writing stuck at band 5 or lower, including 1.

96
00:07:21,130 --> 00:07:24,430
Explanations and examples do not clarify the main

97
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:27,390
ideas of body paragraphs and the writer's opinion.

98
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:32,130
And 2. In the body paragraph, there is some information

99
00:07:32,130 --> 00:07:34,690
not relevant to the main ideas of them.

100
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:38,430
As mentioned earlier, to improve this essay,

101
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:42,310
we should choose the partly agree approach to talk about both sides.

102
00:07:43,050 --> 00:07:45,410
Each will be written in one body paragraph.

103
00:07:46,490 --> 00:07:49,290
Here, I'll improve the writing in three steps.

104
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:54,190
Step 1. In the thesis statement, identify which side 

105
00:07:54,190 --> 00:07:56,870
you will support more and develop it in body 2.

106
00:07:57,550 --> 00:08:00,010
Write about the other side in body 1.

107
00:08:00,810 --> 00:08:03,170
For example, if you show that you support the side,

108
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:09,650
schools still have some responsibility to teach children good behaviours, more in the new thesis statement,

109
00:08:09,650 --> 00:08:14,310
you should develop this main idea in body paragraph 2.

110
00:08:14,550 --> 00:08:19,290
Step 2. Based on the table of brainstormed ideas, 

111
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:22,630
choose the suitable ones to develop each of the main ideas.

112
00:08:23,350 --> 00:08:25,730
Now, I'll instruct you with body 1.

113
00:08:26,750 --> 00:08:29,570
We have main idea for body 1.

114
00:08:30,350 --> 00:08:34,090
Schools not solely responsible for teaching children good manners.

115
00:08:34,870 --> 00:08:37,409
To explain this idea, we look at the

116
00:08:37,409 --> 00:08:40,190
disagree column in the list of ideas and

117
00:08:40,190 --> 00:08:41,770
choose the following ideas.

118
00:08:42,669 --> 00:08:46,290
Parents are closer to their children so provide

119
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:48,610
more moral guidance more effectively.

120
00:08:49,390 --> 00:08:52,510
Large class sizes make it difficult for teachers

121
00:08:52,510 --> 00:08:54,650
to tailor to each child's character.

122
00:08:55,470 --> 00:08:59,670
Remember, you don't need to write about all the brainstormed ideas.

123
00:09:00,190 --> 00:09:02,970
Only choose about one or two ideas that

124
00:09:02,970 --> 00:09:05,270
are easy to write about so that you

125
00:09:05,270 --> 00:09:07,790
can avoid having too many ideas to develop

126
00:09:07,790 --> 00:09:09,850
and not having enough time.

127
00:09:10,970 --> 00:09:16,370
Step 3. Provide an example to specify each idea you have chosen above.

128
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:19,890
To illustrate the explanation, I have an example.

129
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:24,290
A single lesson on gratitude at school, 

130
00:09:24,290 --> 00:09:28,050
not as effective as parents' constant reminders of being thankful.

131
00:09:29,370 --> 00:09:32,670
So, we've developed the main idea stated at

132
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:35,370
the beginning of the paragraph with the following outline.

133
00:09:36,310 --> 00:09:37,310
Topic sentence.

134
00:09:37,970 --> 00:09:41,590
Schools not solely responsible for teaching children good manners.

135
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:43,630
Explanation.

136
00:09:43,930 --> 00:09:48,750
Large class sizes, difficult for teachers to tailor to each child's character.

137
00:09:50,130 --> 00:09:50,950
Elaboration.

138
00:09:51,570 --> 00:09:56,550
Parents are closer to their children so provide moral guidance more effectively.

139
00:09:57,710 --> 00:09:58,490
Example.

140
00:09:58,950 --> 00:10:01,810
A single lesson on gratitude at school is

141
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:05,790
not as effective as parents' constant reminders of being thankful.

142
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:09,050
Now it's your turn.

143
00:10:09,890 --> 00:10:12,650
I have a main idea for body two as follows.

144
00:10:13,330 --> 00:10:16,350
The great impact of schools on students leads

145
00:10:16,350 --> 00:10:19,090
to the school's duty to teach good manners.

146
00:10:20,110 --> 00:10:22,690
Please pause the video for two minutes to

147
00:10:22,690 --> 00:10:25,490
choose an appropriate explanation from the list of ideas 

148
00:10:25,490 --> 00:10:30,070
that we've brainstormed in the previous part and provide an example for it.

149
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:36,740
Alright, have you finished?

150
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,800
Here is my suggested answer.

151
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,740
With the main idea two, the great impact

152
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:46,580
of schools on students leads to the school's

153
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:49,420
duty to teach students good manners, 

154
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,660
